<LegalLayout
  lang="en"
  title="Privacy Policy · Michael Boiman"
  description="Privacy information for this website and the AI chat assistant."
>
  <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p class="legal-updated">Last updated: September 2026</p>

  <p class="legal-muted">
    {/* The article and the link stay on ONE line. With the link on the next
        line Astro dropped the whitespace between them and the page rendered
        "TheGerman version", measured in dist, not guessed from the source. */}
    This is an English courtesy translation. <a href="/de/datenschutz/">The German version</a> is legally authoritative.
  </p>

  <p>
    This website (<strong>mboiman.github.io</strong>) is a personal CV site with an
    optional AI chat assistant. Personal data is processed only to the minimal extent
    described below. There is <strong>no tracking, no advertising and no analytics
    cookies</strong>.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Controller</h2>
  <address>
    Michael Boiman<br />
    Zum Gottschalkhof 2<br />
    60594 Frankfurt am Main, Germany<br />
    Email: <a href="mailto:mboiman@gmail.com">mboiman@gmail.com</a>
  </address>

  <h2>2. Visiting the website (hosting)</h2>
  <p>
    The site is served as a static page via <strong>GitHub Pages</strong> (GitHub,
    Inc., 88 Colin P. Kelly Jr. Street, San Francisco, CA 94107, USA). When you visit,
    GitHub processes technically necessary access data (including IP address, date and
    time, the resource requested, amount of data transferred, browser type) in order
    to deliver the page and keep operation secure and stable. The legal basis is
    Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR (legitimate interest in secure, functional provision).
  </p>

  <h2>3. AI chat assistant</h2>
  <p>
    The site offers an optional chat assistant. Use is voluntary, your input is only
    processed if you send a message yourself.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Processing of messages:</strong> Your input is sent to the agent
      endpoint <em>mboiman.bks-lab.com</em>. The reply is generated by a language
      model from <strong>Anthropic</strong> (Anthropic PBC, San Francisco, USA,
      "Claude"); the agent runs for this on a computer belonging to Michael Boiman,
      which forwards the request to the model. Transport runs through
      <strong>Cloudflare</strong> (Cloudflare, Inc., USA), which processes technical
      connection data (including IP address) to protect the service against abuse
      and overload.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>What travels with a message:</strong> Alongside your input, technical
      details about the page context are transmitted: the path of the open page, the
      selected interface language, the section currently in view, and that page's
      anchors. They let the agent point at a specific place in the CV in its reply.
      No personal details about you and no content from other websites are sent.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Fetching the agent card:</strong> On the pages that display the agent's
      reachability status, its public agent card (<em>agent-card.json</em>) is fetched
      once as the page loads, without any action on your part. Your IP address is
      transmitted to the endpoint named above in doing so. No input is sent and
      nothing is stored in your browser. On every other page, including the legal
      notice and this privacy notice, that fetch does not happen.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Storage of the conversation:</strong> For the duration of the session
      the conversation sits in the agent's memory. Since 6 August 2026, every turn
      is also logged permanently: the question, the answer, a conversation
      identifier, its position in the conversation and how long the reply took, in
      plain text, in an Elastic Cloud environment held under a BKS-Lab GmbH account.
      Separately, the operational logs carry only technical details, never
      conversation content (see section 5 for retention periods).
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Local browser storage:</strong> To operate the chat, a technical session
      identifier is stored in your browser's local storage so a conversation can
      continue across a page reload. It is created when you send your first message,
      not when the page loads. This storage is technically necessary
      (§ 25(2) no. 2 TTDSG) and is not used for tracking. No analytics or advertising
      cookies are set.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Contact and appointment requests:</strong> If you actively make a
      request, the details you provide (e.g. name, contact method, topic, preferred
      date, message) are stored locally as a file together with the most recent
      conversation turns, and forwarded by email over Microsoft 365 (sender
      <em>ai@bks-lab.com</em>) to Michael Boiman. A daily overview of open
      conversations is likewise sent to Michael Boiman; if the system detects an
      abuse attempt, a silent report goes to him without anything being shown to you.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Capacity information:</strong> If you ask about current availability,
      the agent reads a workload figure that Michael Boiman has set. No details
      about you are processed for this.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Office-hours booking (where offered):</strong> If the agent offers an
      office-hours slot and you confirm it, you receive a time-limited confirmation
      code by email and, once an appointment is actually made, a calendar invitation.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Telegram notification (where enabled):</strong> Where this feature is
      active, Michael Boiman receives a notification about new conversations over
      Telegram (Telegram FZ-LLC). Your contact details are not transmitted to
      Telegram.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Weekly review of unanswered questions:</strong> The stored conversation
      logs are automatically reviewed for questions the agent could not answer
      satisfactorily. The result of this review goes only to Michael Boiman and
      serves to improve the agent.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Technical session files of the agent:</strong> While handling a
      request, the agent creates local, technical session files (no content beyond
      what the conversation log already holds).
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    The legal basis for operating the chat, its logging, and the review to improve
    the agent is Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR (legitimate interest in answering questions about
    me and my work, and in a reliable, secure operation); for transmitting contact
    details as part of a request or an office-hours booking, Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR
    (pre-contractual steps) or Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR (consent by sending).
  </p>
  <p class="legal-muted">
    Note: Please do not enter special categories of personal data (e.g. health,
    religious or political data) into the chat, and keep confidential details to
    what your request actually needs, since the conversation is stored as described
    in sections 3 and 5.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Recipients and transfers to third countries</h2>
  <p>
    Within the scope described, data is transferred to the following services:
    <strong>GitHub</strong> (hosting, USA), <strong>Cloudflare</strong> (transport
    and protection of the chat, USA) and <strong>Anthropic</strong> (AI responses,
    USA). Conversation logs sit in an <strong>Elastic Cloud</strong> environment
    held under a BKS-Lab GmbH account; requests, appointment wishes and
    office-hours confirmations are sent over <strong>Microsoft 365</strong>
    (Microsoft Corporation), each in the data-centre region that account uses. Where
    the Telegram notification is enabled, <strong>Telegram</strong> (Telegram
    FZ-LLC) receives a message without your contact details. Where any of this
    processing takes place in a country outside the EU/EEA, it rests on the EU-U.S.
    Data Privacy Framework (where the respective company is certified) or the EU
    Standard Contractual Clauses pursuant to Art. 46 GDPR. No data is passed on to
    any other third parties.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Retention period</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Conversation logs (Elastic):</strong> 90 days.</li>
    <li><strong>Operational logs without conversation content:</strong> 30 days.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>Appointment wishes, requests and office-hours bookings:</strong>
      12 months; deleted thereafter unless statutory retention obligations apply.
    </li>
    <li><strong>Office-hours confirmation codes:</strong> 24 hours.</li>
    <li><strong>Technical session files of the agent:</strong> 30 days.</li>
    <li><strong>Server access data from hosting:</strong> as determined by GitHub.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>6. Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    You have the right to access (Art. 15), rectification (Art. 16), erasure (Art. 17),
    restriction of processing (Art. 18), data portability (Art. 20) and the right to
    object to processing based on legitimate interests (Art. 21 GDPR). You may withdraw
    any consent given at any time with effect for the future (Art. 7(3) GDPR). An
    informal message to
    <a href="mailto:mboiman@gmail.com">mboiman@gmail.com</a> is sufficient.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Right to lodge a complaint</h2>
  <p>
    You have the right to lodge a complaint with a data protection supervisory
    authority, for example the Hessian Commissioner for Data Protection and Freedom of
    Information, Postfach 3163, 65021 Wiesbaden, Germany.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Changes</h2>
  <p>
    This privacy policy will be updated whenever the service or the legal framework
    changes.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
